/llm_router/.env
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Run output is an artifact, not source. It stays on disk as the durable record
# that replaces expiring hosted traces, and none of it belongs in git -- a run
# is megabytes of log that no one reads back through a diff, and it would sit
# in the history forever. Cite a run by its id from a report; keep the files.
evals/results/runs/

# Same for the per-run post-mortems the trace-reviewer writes. The README that
# explains the directory is prose, and stays.
evals/results/reviews/*
!evals/results/reviews/README.md

# What this machine's accounts have spent, plus the pool snapshot the quota
# panel measures it against. Local state, rewritten as the router runs.
/llm_router/.usage/

# Scratch space for reports, plans and one-off analyses produced while working
# with an agent. Point-in-time artifacts, not maintained state -- what survives
# is the writing that gets promoted into docs/ or evals/results/reports/.
/.claude/artifacts/

# The container's environment file: every provider key plus SERVE_TOKEN.
# `llm_router/.env` above is the same secret in the CLI's location; both are
# excluded from the Docker build context as well (.dockerignore).
/.env

# The default workspace root for `docker compose up`. What the agents are bound
# to is someone else's repository, or a clone of one -- never this one's history.
/workspaces/
